# ORCA input: energy and forces of one ethanol configuration at the level of theory of rMD17.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. The line starting with ! holds the keywords:
#   PBE            exchange-correlation functional (a GGA), Perdew, Burke and Ernzerhof (1996)
#   def2-SVP       basis set, split valence with polarization functions (Weigend and Ahlrichs, 2005)
#   def2/J         auxiliary basis for the RI approximation of the Coulomb integrals (default for GGAs)
#   VeryTightSCF   SCF converged to 1e-9 Hartree, so that the forces carry no convergence noise
#   DefGrid3       the densest standard integration grid of ORCA 5 (rMD17 used Grid7 NoFinalGrid of ORCA 4)
#   EnGrad         compute the energy and its gradient; the gradient is written to <name>.engrad
#
# The geometry follows "* xyz charge multiplicity": neutral (0), closed shell (singlet, 1), positions in Å.
# This configuration is index 4823 of the rMD17 ethanol data (test set of split 1).
#
# Run:  bash orca/run_orca.sh orca/example_ethanol_single_point.inp     (10-30 s on one laptop core)

! PBE def2-SVP def2/J VeryTightSCF DefGrid3 EnGrad

* xyz 0 1
C     -0.2864087200    -0.5292426500     0.0476115700
C     -0.9128728700     0.8836917900     0.2107592800
O      1.0729378200    -0.3867296100    -0.2003471200
H     -0.4707297600    -1.1557898400     0.9854427100
H     -0.7733878300    -1.0469524900    -0.6466075900
H     -1.6332249700     1.0550370400     0.9958763900
H     -0.0522336500     1.5820098900     0.3711647200
H     -1.2028401200     1.2520812400    -0.8059573600
H      1.3910358600     0.2271679100    -0.7985050900
*
